            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Assignment operators",
            "text": "Assignment operators assign values to variables. The basic one is =, which assigns the value on the right to the variable on the left; compound operators such as +=, -=, *= and /= combine an arithmetic operation with assignment."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Assignment operators, starting with a = 10 and b = 5 (each line uses the new a)",
